    "notes": "Each measure is an in-frame contrast: mean red excess R-(G+B)/2 inside the predicted sign rectangle minus the same statistic in two side strips on the same image rows, 16 pixels outside the predicted bounds. The front views are positive controls in the same session: the sign's red lettering must be detectable from the front before the back view can say anything. The back contrast is compared with the front contrast of the same sign, so no absolute colour is used. Version 2 adds an occlusion guard: in each back view the mean gray of the sign rectangle must stay within 10 levels of the side strips, so a back face that is drawn but dark (no visible red) cannot count as not drawn. A dim back face of terrain-like brightness and little red remains undetectable without a two-sided control object; see notes."
